                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm nor an usual fan of the rpg genre, but boy, what a delightful game Stargazer Christmas is. \n\nAs the title suggests, it's a game with a christmas thematic. But, for my surprise, it's a well executed one. I found that the mechanics are simple but they are more than enough for the progress of the game. Within 6h of gameplay, I was able to find myself contemplating at how clever some moments were.\n\nThe story is simple, yet, it is full of jokes and references to a previous game of the developer. While I haven't played that previous game (I think it's Stargazer), I found it fun to see the interation between those chracters.\n\nI think it's a game made for moments when you want to relax, but it also gave me a quite enjoyable and uncommon story while feeding me with some challenging moments.",
